ice"}],"gloss":"meat-rice"},{"surface":"உண்டு","parts":[{"text":"உண்டு","lemma":"உண்","gloss":"eating"}],"gloss":"eating"},{"surface":"வருந்துதொழில்","parts":[{"text":"வருந்து","lemma":"வருந்து","gloss":"wearying"},{"text":"தொழில்","lemma":"தொழில்","gloss":"task"}],"gloss":"wearying task"},{"surface":"அல்லது","parts":[{"text":"அல்லது","lemma":"அல்","gloss":"other than"}],"gloss":"other than"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிறிதுதொழில்","parts":[{"text":"பிறிது","lemma":"பிறிது","gloss":"other"},{"text":"தொழில்","lemma":"தொழில்","gloss":"work"}],"gloss":"other work"},{"surface":"அறியா","parts":[{"text":"அறியா","lemma":"அறி","gloss":"not knowing"}],"gloss":"not knowing"},{"surface":"ஆகலின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆகலின்","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"since they are"}],"gloss":"since they are"},{"surface":"நன்றும்","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"நன்று","gloss":"exceedingly"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"உம்","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"exceedingly"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"மெல்லிய","parts":[{"text":"மெல்லிய","lemma":"மென்மை","gloss":"soft"}],"gloss":"soft"},{"surface":"பெரும","parts":[{"text":"பெரும","lemma":"பெருமான்","gloss":"O Lord"}],"gloss":"O Lord"},{"surface":"தாமே","parts":[{"text":"தாம்","lemma":"தாம்","gloss":"they"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed they"},{"surface":"நல்லவர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"நல்லவர்","lemma":"நல்லவர்","gloss":"good women"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"to (dative)"}],"gloss":"to good women"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆரணங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஆர்","lemma":"ஆர்","gloss":"deep"},{"text":"அணங்கு","lemma":"அணங்கு","gloss":"torment/desire"}],"gloss":"causing deep desire"},{"surface":"ஆகிய","parts":[{"text":"ஆகிய","lemma":"ஆகு","gloss":"who has become"}],"gloss":"who has become"},{"surface":"மார்பின்","parts":[{"text":"மார்பு","lemma":"மார்பு","gloss":"chest"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"இன்","gloss":"of (genitive)"}],"gloss":"of the chest"},{"surface":"பொருநர்க்கு","parts":[{"text":"பொருநர்","lemma":"பொருநர்","gloss":"enemies"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"க்கு","gloss":"to (dative)"}],"gloss":"to enemies"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இருநிலத்து","parts":[{"text":"இரு","lemma":"இரு","gloss":"vast"},{"text":"நிலத்து","lemma":"நிலம்","gloss":"earth (oblique)"}],"gloss":"of the vast earth"},{"surface":"அன்ன","parts":[{"text":"அன்ன","lemma":"அன்ன","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"},{"surface":"நோன்மை","parts":[{"text":"நோன்மை","lemma":"நோன்மை","gloss":"strength/endurance"}],"gloss":"strength"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செருமிகு","parts":[{"text":"செரு","lemma":"செரு","gloss":"battle"},{"text":"மிகு","lemma":"மிகு","gloss":"victorious"}],"gloss":"victorious in battle"},{"surface":"சேஎய்","parts":[{"text":"சேஎய்","lemma":"சேய்","gloss":"O Murukaṉ-like lord"}],"gloss":"O Murukaṉ-like lord"},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"நீ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"},{"surface":"பாடுநர்","parts":[{"text":"பாடுநர்","lemma":"பாடுநர்","gloss":"singers"}],"gloss":"singers"},{"surface":"கையே","parts":[{"text":"கை","lemma":"கை","gloss":"hand"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"hands indeed"}]}],"literal":"With fierce-eyed killer elephants / breaking the protective wooden bolts / with gold-crafted elephant goads / driving with strength and withstanding battle / reining in fast horses leaping / aiming at the water expanse of deep moats dug in the earth / from the chariot, reaching the back where the quiver rests / discharging arrows until the strong bowstring leaves scars / and bestowing precious ornaments to recipients of gifts, O Lord / strong are your knee-touching broad hands! / Eating fresh pieces of meat smelling of flesh / seasoned with flower-fragrant smoke, and meat sauce / with meat-rice, which is a wearying task, other than that / not knowing any other work, therefore, exceedingly / soft, O Lord, are they indeed! To good women / causing deep desire with your chest, to enemies / having the strength like the vast earth / O Murukaṉ-like lord victorious in battle, the hands of those who sing your praises!","translation":"O Lord, your broad hands that reach down to your knees are mighty! They have broken the protective wooden bolts of enemy fortresses using fierce-eyed killer elephants. With gold-adorned goads, they have driven those beasts forward to withstand the fury of battle. They have reined in swift horses as they leaped across deep, water-filled moats dug into the earth. Standing upon your chariot, they have reached back to the quiver to discharge arrows, bearing the scars of the strong bowstring. And they have generously bestowed precious ornaments upon those who come seeking gifts. But the hands of those who sing your praises, O Great Lord, are exceedingly soft! For they know no other work than the wearying task of eating rich meat-rice, enjoying fresh pieces of meat that smell of flesh, seasoned with flower-fragrant smoke and thick meat sauce. O Murukaṉ-like lord, victorious in battle! Your chest inspires deep desire in good women, but to your enemies, it stands with the endurance of the vast earth. Truly, the hands of your singers are soft, while yours are strong!","modern":"சினங்கொண்ட கொலைக் களிறுகளைக் கொண்டு, பகைவர்களின் கோட்டை வாயிலின் காவற் கதவுகளின் மரக் கணையங்களை உடைத்து, பொன்னால் செய்யப்பட்ட அங்குசத்தைக் கொண்டு வலிமையுடன் அவற்றை நடத்திப் போரைத் தாங்கியும்; நிலத்தைத் தோண்டி அமைத்த ஆழமான அகழியின் நீர்ப் பரப்பைக் கடந்து பாயும் குதிரைகளை அடக்கியும்; தேரின் மீது நின்றுகொண்டு, முதுகில் உள்ள அம்பறாத்தூணியிலிருந்து அம்புகளை எடுத்து, வில்லின் வலிய நாண் வடுவை உண்டாக்குமாறு செலுத்தியும்; இரவலர்களுக்கு அரிய அணிகலன்களை வழங்கியும் விளங்கும் உனது முழங்கால் வரை நீண்ட பெரிய கைகள் வலிமையானவை, தலைவனே! ஆனால், உன்னைப் பாடும் பாணர்களின் கைகளோ, புலால் நாற்றமுடைய பசிய இறைச்சித் துண்டுகளை, மலர் மணம் கமழும் புகையூட்டிச் சமைத்த இறைச்சிக் குழம்பையும் கறிச்சோற்றையும் உண்டு மகிழும் வருத்தத்தைத் தரும் தொழிலைத் தவிர வேறு எந்தத் தொழிலையும் அறியாதவை. ஆதலால், அவை மிகவும் மென்மையானவை, பெருமானே! நல்ல பெண்களுக்கு அணங்கு போன்ற ஆசையைத் தரும் மார்பையும், பகைவர்களுக்குப் பரந்த நிலத்தைப் போன்ற பொறுமையையும் வலிமையையும் கொண்ட, போரில் சிறந்த முருகனைப் போன்றவனே! உன்னைப் பாடுவோரின் கைகள் மிகவும் மென்மையானவை!","explanation":"The poet Kapilar is praising the Cēra king Celvak Kaṭuṅkō Vāḻiyātaṉ. He contrasts the hard, scarred, and powerful hands of the king with the soft, delicate hands of his bards. The king's hands are hardened by battle—breaking fortress gates with elephants, reining in swift horses over deep moats, shooting arrows until scarred by the bowstring, and constantly giving away precious gifts. In contrast, the bards' hands are soft because they have no other work than the 'wearying' task of eating the rich, fragrant meat-rice and delicacies provided by the king's hospitality. This poem belongs to the pāṭāṇ tiṇai (praising a king's exploits and generosity). The vivid descriptions of warfare highlight the king's heroism, while the sensory details of the feast emphasize his immense patronage.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}